\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Beat-aligned occlusion of the ECG term over 120 high-risk training ECGs of patients with an event. Windows are fixed offsets from the R peak. Each window lists the centres of the 24~ms occlusions it groups and the span of the beat that their occluded samples cover, from the start of the first sample to the end of the last. Each centre is rounded to a whole sample towards the R peak. The raw value is the mean drop in log-risk, with negative means set to zero, and the normalised value is that drop per unit of signal energy removed.}}{21}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:occlusion}{{5}{21}{Beat-aligned occlusion of the ECG term over 120 high-risk training ECGs of patients with an event. Windows are fixed offsets from the R peak. Each window lists the centres of the 24~ms occlusions it groups and the span of the beat that their occluded samples cover, from the start of the first sample to the end of the last. Each centre is rounded to a whole sample towards the R peak. The raw value is the mean drop in log-risk, with negative means set to zero, and the normalised value is that drop per unit of signal energy removed}{table.5}{}}
